# {{ project_name }}

Built with [GreatAPI](https://github.com/sahajrajmalla/greatapi).

## Run it

```bash
cp .env.example .env          # already contains a generated secret key
greatapi migrate              # create the database schema
greatapi createsuperuser      # an account for the admin
greatapi runserver
```

| URL | What |
|---|---|
| <http://127.0.0.1:8000/> | your API |
| <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs> | OpenAPI docs |
| <http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin> | the admin |

## Add an app

```bash
greatapi startapp blog
greatapi makemigrations -m "add blog"
greatapi migrate
```

`startapp` registers the app in `{{ project_name }}/settings.py`, so its models,
admin classes and router are picked up with no further wiring.

## Layout

```
{{ project_name }}/settings.py   INSTALLED_APPS
main.py                          the application
migrations/                      Alembic revisions
.env                             configuration (git-ignored)
```

## Useful commands

```bash
greatapi routes                        # every route in the app
greatapi makemigrations -m "message"   # generate a migration from model changes
greatapi migrate                       # apply migrations
greatapi downgrade -1                  # roll one back
greatapi generate-secret               # a fresh signing key
```
